  "body": "## Summary\n\n- Report nonempty `CARGO_BUILD_TARGET` and dynamic `CARGO_TARGET_<triple>_RUSTFLAGS` inputs. Preserve their values and the selected target.\n- Report selected Cargo config paths from the plan's command directories, their ancestors, and Cargo home. Add ordinary rustflags, target and profile key hints.\n- Repeat the captured diagnostics in the gate summary. Do not print configuration values.\n- Apply the existing unit environment policy to the docs-images Cargo command.\n- Test real inherited profile removal in isolated child processes. Inspect the renderer command without starting the renderer.\n\nEvery selected config file gets a warning, even without a recognized key. The hints are not effective configuration. Cargo still resolves precedence. The scan does not expand inline tables, escaped key names, includes, or multiline strings. No absence of a hint proves absence of an input. The decision record explains this conservative policy and the rejected alternatives.\n\n## Readings and ownership\n\n- Issue #3155 and its complete current thread.\n- Current upstream rules, ownership procedure, and the original unit-environment change in `f10e123f8`.\n- Started from upstream main `159ee374855281904e1fb3ea7069a4eee61568f8` after updating the recorded base.\n- Writer record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3155#issuecomment-7222723344\n- Base update: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3155#issuecomment-7222791990\n\n## Verification\n\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: PASS on the committed tree. The selected xtask tests and integration tests pass. The unit binary has 373 passing tests.\n- Focused unit-environment and docs-command tests: PASS. New target diagnostics, config diagnostics, renderer pinning and summary tests first failed without their implementations.\n- Negative control: disabling profile removal makes the inherited-profile regression fail. Restoring removal makes it pass.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test -p xtask -j 3 --test docs_images`: PASS, including the committed-image check and the new gate-summary check.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -j 3 -- -D warnings`: FAIL on the pre-existing Linux `clippy::needless_bool` at unchanged `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67`. This PR does not change that file.\n- Supplemental Clippy with only `-A clippy::needless_bool` after `-D warnings`: PASS. This is not a strict Clippy pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --dry-run`: the plan was inspected. It selects release builds of motion and app, not an xtask light twin. Those release steps were not run for this tooling-only change.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n\nThe first full quick run exceeded a 300-second tool wait after the unit tests passed. A longer wait completed the full gate. The final committed-tree run also passed.\n\n## Limits\n\nNo application, example-catalog, GUI-renderer or release rebuild was used for the command-construction proof. No images, fixtures, CAM algorithms or user configuration were changed. Linux execution does not prove Windows runtime behavior or machine safety. No independent upstream approval or green CI result is claimed. Maintainer review and merge remain outside this contribution.\n\nEffort: low\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: The gate reports preserved target and Cargo config inputs; docs-images uses the fixed unit environment.\n\nFixes #3155\n",
